# Besides the usual same-cycle cross-module ordering (which sort_output would
# handle), verilator drops the final "Data enqued" $display: that display and
# the $finish land in the same timestamp, and verilator's deferred $finish
# stops the run before emitting it, whereas iverilog/Bluesim complete the
# timestamp.  Both behaviors are legal (whether $finish aborts the remaining
# same-time events is implementation-defined), but we prefer the Bluesim-
# equivalent variant that emits the full timestamp.  Because the design's
# deq_out and enq displays both fire every cycle in separately-synthesized
# modules, there is no display-free cycle on which $finish could fire, so this
# cannot be reshaped into a pure reorder; the missing line is XFAILed under
# verilator (sorting cannot reconcile a missing line).
test_veri_only_bsv_multi Testbench mkTestbench {mkTop mkDesign} "mkTestbench.v.out.expected" verilator
test_c_only_bsv_multi Testbench mkTestbench {mkTop mkDesign} "mkTestbench.c.out.expected"
